<body>

<h1>Human Interface Design (Screens)</h1>

<h2>5.2 Overview of the User Interface</h2>

<p>The user interface (UI) is part of a software program or device that users see and interact with. It controls how users use the program or website and how information appears on the screen. UI focuses on making the design clear, easy to use, and visually appealing so users have a better experience. The system will be used by two primary types of users: Admin/Staff (Administrators and Plumbers) and Customers.</p>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 30%;">Use Case</th>
            <th style="width: 70%;">Details</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Login</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff and Customers can login into the system by using a registered email and password.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Manage Account</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff and Customers can manage user accounts (create, view, update, and delete) with details such as name, email, phone number, address, and password.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Manage Booking</strong></td>
            <td>Customers can create, view, and cancel booking appointments with details such as service type, date, time slot, problem description, and attachments; Admin/Staff can view, update booking status, and assign plumbers.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Manage Payment</strong></td>
            <td>Customers can create payment entries by uploading deposit receipts and view payment statuses; Admin/Staff can review, approve, or reject payment receipts and update verification statuses.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Manage Refund</strong></td>
            <td>Customers can initiate refund requests upon booking cancellation and view refund statuses; Admin/Staff can view, process refund settlements, and upload proof transfer slips.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Manage Job Record</strong></td>
            <td>Plumbers/Staff can log completed service job records (create, view, and update) with details such as completion date, total cost, replaced parts, and service notes; Customers can view their job completion summaries.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Generate Report</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff can generate and view business performance analytics, revenue reports, booking count statistics, and monthly sales performance charts.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Manage Feedback</strong></td>
            <td>Customers can submit ratings, review comments, and feedback photos for completed jobs; Customers and Admin/Staff can view feedback review boards and staff replies.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Manage Chat & Communication</strong></td>
            <td>Customers and Admin/Staff can send and view real-time chat messages for active booking sessions, and view system push notifications for real-time status updates.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Detailed Use Case Interface Mapping (All 24 Use Cases)</h2>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 30%;">Use Case</th>
            <th style="width: 70%;">Details</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Login</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff and Customers can login into the system using their registered email address and password.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Create Account</strong></td>
            <td>New customers can register a profile account, or Admins can register a new plumber/staff profile with details such as name, email, phone, address, and password.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>View Account</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff and Customers can view their profile account details including personal information, contact number, and address.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Update Account</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff and Customers can update their personal profile details, phone number, address, or password credentials.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Delete Account</strong></td>
            <td>Admins can delete/deactivate plumber staff accounts, or customers can deactivate their profile.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Create Booking</strong></td>
            <td>Customers can reserve a new plumbing service appointment by choosing a service type, date, time slot, and describing the issue.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>View Booking</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff and Customers can view past or pending booking appointment details, schedule dates, and status badges.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Update Booking</strong></td>
            <td>Staff/Admins can update booking status (e.g. In Progress, Completed), reschedule dates, or assign plumbers; Customers can edit pending booking details.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Delete Booking</strong></td>
            <td>Customers can cancel an existing booking appointment, which automatically calculates deposit refund eligibility.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Create Payment</strong></td>
            <td>Customers can upload bank transfer deposit receipt screenshots to confirm an appointment schedule.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>View Payment</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff and Customers can view payment transaction details, receipt image previews, verification statuses, and download PDF receipts.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Update Payment</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff can verify, approve (assigning a plumber) or reject payment receipts with explanatory notes.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Create Refund</strong></td>
            <td>System/Customers generate a refund application record when an eligible paid booking is cancelled.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>View Refund</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff and Customers can view refund application details, calculated refund amounts, and status updates.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Update Refund</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff can upload bank transfer refund proof slips, enter remarks, and mark refund status as completed.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Create Job Record</strong></td>
            <td>Plumbers/Staff can create a job record detailing work performed, total completion cost, materials used, and service notes upon completing a job.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>View Job Record</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff and Customers can inspect completed job summaries, itemized billing cost breakdowns, and invoice summaries.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Update Job Record</strong></td>
            <td>Plumbers/Staff can edit existing job record details, adjust total cost figures, or update service notes.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Generate Report</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff can view business performance analytics, monthly revenue charts, booking statistics, and sales reports.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Create Feedback</strong></td>
            <td>Customers can submit star ratings, review comments, and feedback photos after a job is completed; Staff can post response comments.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>View Feedback</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff and Customers can view customer reviews, star ratings, and staff replies on the review board.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Create Chat Message</strong></td>
            <td>Customers and Admin/Staff can exchange real-time chat messages regarding active booking details and inquiries.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>View Chat Messages</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff and Customers can view the chat conversation timeline for a specific booking and mark unread messages as read.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>View Push Notifications</strong></td>
            <td>Admin/Staff and Customers can view real-time in-app notification alerts regarding booking updates, payment approvals, and chat messages.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

</body>
</html>
